	(text "Those pads are not connected as they are\non the Low Voltage side of the HV board\nand Earth needs at least 3 to 6mm of \nisolation with Low voltage signals"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 130.048 30.226 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0147b482-ffd9-4238-a3c6-0d0143a0582d")
	)
	(text "13-11-2026 (dd-mm-yyyy)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 221.742 193.294 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0872896f-fd5a-4532-82b5-fcd590d6e120")
	)
	(text "Note: this wire could go through a current sensing transformer attached\nto its burden resistor, in order to read live current figures.\nThis can be very useful to calculate the average current being drawn by the \nresistive elements, and thus compute the oven's real power.\n\nNote2: Real power can be computed as the heating elements are behaving as purely resistive loads, \nhence not contributing to phase shift between the current/voltage signals."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 179.07 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0ab9c01d-38d4-4478-92ac-484fcd54a529")
	)
	(text "Adapted to a 5V rail (VSys is connected\nto USB 5V charger in series with a schottky diode\nwith a forward voltage drop of around 0.9V Max"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 105.41 70.866 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.889 0.889)
			)
		)
		(uuid "1b3a935b-fc50-4949-8821-831411c4f6ae")
	)
	(text "High voltage board, including the switching element. This board was recovered (and arranged) from the early design \nin NanoFridgeThermostat High Voltage daughter board and is completely optional (it can be detached from an original \nNanoFridgeThermostat V2 PCB or manually crafted out of prototype boards, as long as you respect HV / LV isolation \nand use at least 1.5mm² wires or wide traces (>= 6mm).\n\nNote: this version provides a larger PCB with support for heatsink pins, as the original NanoFridgeThermostat board \ndid not face the same load. The triac will see a max avg current of about 6.5 Amps (heating elements are rated \nat 1500W @ 230V), hence power dissipation will be around 9 - 10 Watts. \nA good heatsink ( <= 7K/W ) with proper ventilation will be required."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8 173.736 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "52b71f5d-a3cc-4999-87b5-933f19b1e852")
	)
	(text "1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 269.494 193.294 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "8f038472-5a12-42c1-be8c-fb4317561aba")
	)
	(text "Pico Reflow Oven High Voltage daughter board"
